  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency agricultural livelihoods assistance for drought affected communities in Afar, Amhara and Tigray regions</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this WFP project is to save lives and livelihoods of vulnerable drought affected communities in Afar, Amhara and Tigray regions of Ethiopia. This assistance will enables the beneficiaries to increase food availability and access, and protects livestock assets to increase availability and access to livestock products including milk and meat and ensure improved food and nutrition security of the targeted households. The project provides life-saving assistance to 415,000  people, including 96,280 women, 94, 620 men,  112,050 children, and  74,700 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
